{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w7jf6pjzqgspjkoiilgwykfnt7gfsym3cjzmnrk4jv4xqa6hgloa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Final state:\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe project is a single-translation-unit cJSON-derived number parser (`parse_number`, 114 lines of C). No `[features]` in `Cargo.toml` and no `option()` in `CMakeLists.txt` → **one build configuration**, verified across both `--no-default-features` and default × debug and release (4 combinations).\n\n**Two genuine divergences found**, both invisible to happy-path testing:\n\n| trigger | C | Rust (before) | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `item == NULL` on the **success** path (the C never null-checks `item`) | SIGSEGV (11) | **SIGABRT (6)** — rustc's `-C debug-assertions` null-deref UB check turned the fault into a non-unwinding panic | route the three `item` stores through `write_unaligned` |\n| **misaligned** `cJSON *` / `parse_buffer *` (legal for the C; nothing promises alignment) | succeeds, exit 0 | **SIGABRT (6)** — debug alignment UB check aborted on an access the C performs happily | route every `item`/`input_buffer` field access through `read_unaligned`/`write_unaligned` |\n\nAlso hardened three UB-adjacent spots (`content.add(offset)` → `wrapping_add` for `offset >= length`; skip the zero-length `memcpy`; `wrapping_add` for the scan index since callers may lie about `length`).\n\n## Artifacts (all verified on disk)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` diff is **empty** in both profiles (C exports 1 symbol, Rust exports the same 1); `ldd -r` reports zero unresolved symbols; full C-entity→Rust mapping table showing nothing was left untranslated.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 23 rows, **all `[x]`**, derived by grepping every `return`, null check, and limit constant. Includes all 3 reachable `return false` sites, both saturation limits, out-of-range `type` enum values across FFI, `SIZE_MAX` offset wraparound, embedded NUL.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 31 rows, **all `[x]`**, from 12 axes the C actually branches on.\n- **`MUTANTS.md`** — harness self-check: 35 injected bugs, **32 killed**; the 3 survivors are proven *equivalent* mutants, each with a dedicated justification test (NaN arm is dead code — verified over 813,615 exhaustive inputs; `offset+index` can never overflow; the `'.'`-rewrite loop is a no-op since `decimal_point == '.'`).\n\n## Test suite — 66 tests, all passing in all 4 configurations\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and called only through their exported `parse_number`. Key harness properties: an **in-charset digit read guard** just past `length` (so any over-read changes the result instead of reading a harmless heap byte — this is what converts the off-by-one mutants from \"survived\" to \"killed\"), poisoned out-parameters, bitwise `f64` comparison, and per-implementation buffer copies. Coverage includes **exhaustive** enumeration of every charset string of length ≤ 5 (813,615 inputs), every 256-byte value in leader/terminator/sole positions, the full `(content, length, offset)` matrix for 3-byte inputs, 6-seed × 20,000-case fuzzing, and multi-call sequences sharing one `parse_buffer`.\n\nReproduce with `./verify.sh` (feature/profile matrix + symbol diff) and `./mutants.sh`. `c_src/` is unmodified (`git diff -- c_src` empty)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1949,"cache_read_input_tokens":172919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1949,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72b1309a-1caa-4630-ae5d-a71b32e4dec5","uuid":"dff082c7-c7cf-4ff3-89c4-08bd61632c8c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:39:42.076Z"}
